From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:38:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 17/30] drm/msm: mark fbdev framebuffer as virtual memory

The MSM fbdev screen buffer is a CPU virtual mapping of a GEM object.
Mark it as virtual memory so fbcon uses the appropriate software drawing
helpers.

Signed-off-by: Yassin <yassin@Nixos>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
index 89ca9da3e..0ff567417 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_fbdev.c
@@ -163,6 +163,7 @@ int msm_fbdev_driver_fbdev_probe(struct drm_fb_helper *helper,
 		ret = PTR_ERR(fbi->screen_buffer);
 		goto err_msm_gem_unpin;
 	}
+	fbi->flags |= FBINFO_VIRTFB;
 	fbi->screen_size = bo->size;
 	fbi->fix.smem_start = paddr;
 	fbi->fix.smem_len = bo->size;
